ottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;24.7&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;* California income tax is 100% of the state income tax effect in this rate reconciliation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;BVES&#8217;s policy is to classify interest on income tax over/underpayments in interest income/expense and penalties in &#8220;Other Income Deductions.&#8221; BVES did not have any material interest receivables/payables from/to taxing authorities as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, nor did it recognize any material interest income/expense or accrue any material tax-related penalties during the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;Excess Deferred Federal Income Taxes (EDFIT):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;As the excess deferred tax assets and excess deferred tax liabilities reverse over the amortization period, described below, the net regulatory liability will reverse with offsets to accounts 410.1 (provision for deferred income taxes) and 411.1 (provision for deferred income taxes-credit).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The following table reflects the portion of the ungrossed EDFIT balance that is protected and the portion that is unprotected as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, along with the amounts associated with the 2025 reversal and elimination of ADIT balances in the regulatory liability account (amounts in thousands):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:77.678%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:25.145%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:22.654%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:23.995%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:23.806%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;text-indent:5.6pt;vertical-align:middle"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:83%"&gt;Jurisdiction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;text-indent:24.7pt;vertical-align:middle"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:83%"&gt;12/31/2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:83%"&gt;Balance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;text-indent:24.7pt;vertical-align:middle"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:83%"&gt;Amortization to Deferred Provision&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;text-indent:24.7pt;vertical-align:middle"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:83%"&gt;12/31/2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:83%"&gt;Balance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;text-indent:5.6pt;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:83%"&gt;Protected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style=